Element of Java used: Polymorphism - method (function) overloading.

class Shape
{
    void area(double b, double h)              // triangle
    {
        System.out.println("Area of triangle = " + 0.5 * b * h);
    }

    void area(double s)                        // square
    {
        System.out.println("Area of square = " + s * s);
    }

    void area(double h, double a, double b)    // trapezium
    {
        System.out.println("Area of trapezium = " + 0.5 * h * (a + b));
    }

    void area(int l, int b)                    // rectangle
    {
        System.out.println("Area of rectangle = " + l * b);
    }

    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        Shape ob = new Shape();
        ob.area(6.0, 4.0);        // triangle: 12.0
        ob.area(5.0);             // square: 25.0
        ob.area(4.0, 3.0, 5.0);   // trapezium: 16.0
        ob.area(7, 3);            // rectangle: 21
    }
}
(The four methods share the name area but differ in the number or type of parameters, so the compiler chooses the correct one from the arguments.)

import java.util.Scanner;

class Password
{
    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the password: ");
        String pw = sc.nextLine();
        int i, l = pw.length(), uc = 0, lc = 0, d = 0, sp = 0;
        char ch;
        for (i = 0; i < l; i++)
        {
            ch = pw.charAt(i);
            if (Character.isUpperCase(ch))
                uc++;
            else if (Character.isLowerCase(ch))
                lc++;
            else if (Character.isDigit(ch))
                d++;
            else
                sp++;                       // special character
        }
        if (l >= 12 && uc >= 4 && lc >= 4 && d >= 2 && sp >= 2)
            System.out.println("Strong password");
        else
            System.out.println("Not a strong password");
    }
}

Trace: "ABCDabcd12@#" -> length 12, 4 upper, 4 lower, 2 digits, 2 special -> Strong password.
"Abcd1234@#xy" -> only 1 upper case letter -> Not a strong password.
